  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/esa-limited-capability-work
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source explicitly separates the hardship test from the WCA rather than treating one finding as evidence of the other.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol9-ch53/0031
      quote: "53141 Hardship is not defined in the law. It should therefore be given its normal everyday meaning 1 of\n“severe suffering or privation”. Privation means a lack of the necessities of life.\n\n\nNote: The test for hardship is not related to the WCA which is the functional assessment to determine\neligibility for ESA. A claimant is judged to be in hardship if they have insufficient funds to meet their\nimmediate, essential and basic necessities of life, i.e. accommodation, food, heating and lighting, clothing\nand hygiene requirements.\n\n\n                                                                                                 1 R(SB) 19/82"
      locator: DMG 53141
  - target: term/dmg-evidence-assessment
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source requires the reasons, factors and evidence, including reasons for accepting or rejecting evidence, to be recorded.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol9-ch53/0032
      quote: "53150 DMs should record\n\n\n1. the reasons why hardship will or will not occur and\n\n\n2. the factors and evidence considered\n\n\nas part of the decision on hardship payments."
      locator: DMG 53150
    - page: page/dmg-vol9-ch53/0032
      quote: "53151 DMs must record their reasons for\n\n\n1. rejecting any evidence or\n\n\n2. deciding what evidence to accept if faced with conflicting evidence.\n\n\n\nWhen a hardship payment is made"
      locator: DMG 53151
